REA Notes search grammar study — source-only proposal

This study inspects Joplin Desktop 3.6.14, tag v3.6.14, commit
7e2765a3857754d12dbadea442b60ceaf9d4b23d in laurent22/joplin.
The four preserved original source/document files carry their upstream notices
and root license. Upstream Joplin copyright (c) 2016-2025 Laurent Cozic,
as specified in the preserved upstream license; no endorsement is
implied. Joplin is a trademark of JOPLIN SAS. No logos or icons are included.

The newly authored grammar, matcher, application changes and tests are informed
by original source inspection, not a clean-room implementation. They are offered
as source-assisted research code under AGPL-3.0-or-later, conservatively matching
the preserved upstream repository license. Copyright 2026 Ginderlax for original
laboratory additions. The preserved COPYING contains the AGPL version3 text.

Original code is retained for documentation and isolated test-only comparisons.
The product runtime does not import or wrap the original parser/search engine.
The prospective test adapters execute the exact pure parser and query-builder
bodies with authenticated source bytes in a supported hosted environment only.
The query-builder adapter replaces only its unused date-service import with a
deny-on-access adapter and compares metadata-only SQL on synthetic SQLite.
They do not execute the full original application, database lifecycle or GUI.

No candidate/original source, tests, products, builds or syntax checks have run
in this source-authoring stage. No full search parity, performance improvement,
compatibility, accessibility or superiority claim follows from this proposal.
